resolve
@unchecked
Resolves CLI filesystem targets relative to the explicit base directory. Exact
files, ./..., and arbitrary path/... targets are supported. Plain directories
recurse only when recurse_plain_dirs is true. Results are sorted and deduplicated.

A nearest-ancestor .aikiignore supplies [all] and tool-specific rules. The first
matching policy language supports exact repository-relative paths, subtree
prefixes written as path/**, and **/.* for hidden-path pruning. Policy is applied
before descending into discovered directories. A target explicitly rooted inside
an ignored subtree bypasses policy for that target.

Returns [@targets, paths, excluded], where excluded contains policy decisions as
[@target, path, :policy] records. Returns [@error, :target, msg] for invalid or
nonexistent targets.

resolve(base, tool, targets, recurse_plain_dirs)

===

resolve_all
@unchecked
Uses the same target language, ordering, deduplication, and command directory
policy as resolve(), but bypasses .aikiignore. This is the exhaustive repository
selection surface used by CLI --all validation modes. Explicit command filtering
still applies after resolution.

resolve_all(base, tool, targets, recurse_plain_dirs)
